CommitDate: Thu Oct 1 10:15:58 2026 -0500

    fix(S3-GIT-006): bound S3 client request timeout + close inherited flock fd in unified cron. Addresses S3-GIT-006.
    
    The unified S3 sync tree sat VISIBLE-HEALTHY but never finished (frozen
    write_bytes, ESTAB to :443): buildClient set NO request/socket bound, so
    any slow or queued request could pin a run — and with it the unified
    cron's single-instance flock — indefinitely. Every 15-min cron since
    2026-09-30 22:30 spawned a NEW parallel sync tree, both holding fd 9.
    
    Half 1 — src/s3/client.ts: buildClient now wires NodeHttpHandler with
    connectionTimeout 10s, requestTimeout 120s and an https Agent
    (keepAlive, maxSockets 20). A slow leg now REJECTS loudly instead of
    hanging silently. Proven hermetically against localhost:1 (ECONNREFUSED,
    in-process): listRemoteObjects/client.send reject within 15s, and the
    handler config carries the three bounds. A one-shot CLI shape with two
    successful sends against a loopback server exits on its own (keepAlive
    pool unpinned). RED-proven: on the HEAD (unbounded) client the bounds
    cell fails; restored byte-identical.
    
    Half 2 — scripts/s3/duckbrain-s3-unified.sh: children no longer inherit
    the lock fd. The shell takes the flock on fd 9 and every layer
    invocation closes fd 9 for that invocation only (`9>&-`). NOTE: the
    brief's literal `exec 9>&-` after `flock -n 9` RELEASES the lock (the
    flock lives on the open file description and dies with its last fd —
    measured live mid-run: a second flock succeeds while the shell is still
    running), which would have allowed concurrent cron ticks; the
    per-invocation close is the shape that keeps the shell holding the lock
    while spawning clean children. Pinned by scripts/s3/test-fd-inheritance.sh
    (14 arms, hermetic): the wrong shape is asserted to release mid-run so
    it cannot be re-introduced; the end-to-end arm on the REAL unified
    script proves the running child has no lockfile fd, the wrapper shell
    does, a concurrent wrapper SKIPS, and the lock is free after exit.
    RED-proven against the HEAD script: arm5 fails at "child inherited the
    lockfile fd"; restored byte-identical.
    
    Tests: +1 vitest file (4 tests, src/s3/client-timeout-s3git006.test.ts)
    and +1 hermetic shell harness (scripts/s3/test-fd-inheritance.sh).
    AGENTS.md Vitest counts synced to the live suite via
    scripts/sync-agents-md-counts.sh in the same commit (GAP-012 guard).
    
    Verification: pnpm tsc --noEmit clean; pnpm test:run full suite green
    (counts in AGENTS.md updated to the live totals); bash
    scripts/s3/test-push-backoff.sh 85/85 (regression: wrapper runs 4/5/7
    unchanged); bash scripts/s3/test-fd-inheritance.sh 14/14; prettier
    --check clean on touched ts files (bonus: one pre-existing dirty cast
    line in client.ts reformatted); bash -n clean on both scripts.
    
